exd5 9. d4 b6 10. Nbd2 Bb7 11. Rc1 Rc8 12. Re1 Re8 13. a3 Bd6 14. dxc5 bxc5 15.
Bd3 Ne4 16. Qc2 Qe7 17. Nf1 h6 18. Ng3 Nxg3 19. hxg3 Ne5 20. Bxe5 Bxe5 21. Nxe5
Qxe5 22. Qe2 Re6 23. Kf1 Rb6 24. Rb1 c4 25. bxc4 dxc4 26. Bc2 Rcc6 27. Rxb6
Rxb6 28. Qd2 Rd6 29. Qb4 Rb6 30. Qd2 g6 31. Rc1 Rb2 {... no further moves
recorded. "Black went c3 and Rb2, White went Qd8+ and Ba4 to avoid the pin,
and that allowed ...Bxg2+ Kxg2 Qe4+, winning the B on a4. But I was then able
to go Rxc3 and the endgame after that was quickly drawn." (Peter Andrews)}
